{"name":"devtools-smoke","title":"devtools-smoke","description":"","files":{"README.md":"# Triggery DevTools — manual smoke test\n\nStandalone HTML page that wires `@triggery/devtools-bridge` to a runtime and exposes buttons for every panel-relevant scenario (sync fire, async, cascade, skipped, errored, dispose).\n\n> **Not runnable in StackBlitz.** This example requires the unpacked Chrome extension from `extensions/chrome-devtools/`, so the `/play/devtools-smoke/` launcher is intentionally omitted. Run it locally instead.\n>\n> - **Bridge package** — <https://triggeryjs.github.io/packages/devtools-bridge/>\n> - **Panel package** — <https://triggeryjs.github.io/packages/devtools-panel/>\n\n## Run it\n\nFrom the repo root:\n\n```bash\npnpm build               # make sure packages/*/dist exist\npython3 -m http.server 8000\n```\n\nThen in Chrome:\n\n1. `chrome://extensions` → **Developer mode** → **Load unpacked** → select `extensions/chrome-devtools/`.\n2. Open <http://localhost:8000/examples/devtools-smoke/>.\n3. Open DevTools (`⌥⌘I` / `Ctrl+Shift+I`) → switch to the **Triggery** panel.\n4. Click any button — the run shows up in the panel within a few ms.\n\n## What each button should produce in the panel\n\n| Button | Expected panel row |\n|---|---|\n| `fireSync tick` | `fired demo ← tick → notify` |\n| `fire tick (async)` | Same as above, after a microtask tick |\n| `cascade: a → b` | Two rows: `fired t-a ← a → goB` + `fired t-b ← b` |\n| `fire secure (skipped)` | `skipped secure ← secure (missing-required-condition:session)` |\n| `register session condition` | (no panel row — registration only) — next `fire secure` will say `fired` |\n| `unregister session` | (no panel row) — `fire secure` returns to skipped |\n| `fire boom (errored)` | `errored boom ← boom` |\n| `dispose bridge` | Status dot in panel header goes grey; further events stop appearing |\n\nClick any row in the panel to expand the full JSON snapshot.\n","index.html":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n    <title>Triggery devtools smoke test</title>\n    <style>\n      body {\n        font: 14px/1.4 system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;\n        max-width: 720px;\n        margin: 40px auto;\n        padding: 0 16px;\n      }\n      h1 {\n        font-size: 18px;\n      }\n      .row {\n        display: flex;\n        gap: 8px;\n        flex-wrap: wrap;\n        margin: 12px 0;\n      }\n      button {\n        background: #0969da;\n        color: #fff;\n        border: 0;\n        padding: 6px 14px;\n        border-radius: 6px;\n        cursor: pointer;\n        font: inherit;\n      }\n      button.muted {\n        background: #6e7681;\n      }\n      button.warn {\n        background: #cf222e;\n      }\n      pre {\n        background: #f6f8fa;\n        border: 1px solid #d0d7de;\n        padding: 10px;\n        border-radius: 6px;\n        max-height: 320px;\n        overflow: auto;\n        font: 12px/1.4 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;\n      }\n      .hint {\n        color: #57606a;\n        font-size: 12px;\n      }\n    </style>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <h1>Triggery devtools smoke test</h1>\n    <p class=\"hint\">\n      Open Chrome DevTools and switch to the <strong>Triggery</strong> panel. The\n      bridge installs on page load — every button below produces an entry in the\n      panel.\n    </p>\n\n    <div class=\"row\">\n      <button type=\"button\" id=\"tick\">fireSync tick (sync)</button>\n      <button type=\"button\" id=\"async\">fire tick (async, microtask)</button>\n      <button type=\"button\" id=\"cascade\">cascade: a → b</button>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"row\">\n      <button type=\"button\" id=\"skip\" class=\"warn\">fire secure (skipped — no session)</button>\n      <button type=\"button\" id=\"register\" class=\"muted\">register session condition</button>\n      <button type=\"button\" id=\"unregister\" class=\"muted\">unregister session</button>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"row\">\n      <button type=\"button\" id=\"error\" class=\"warn\">fire boom (errored)</button>\n      <button type=\"button\" id=\"dispose\" class=\"muted\">dispose bridge</button>\n    </div>\n\n    <p class=\"hint\">In-page log (mirror, not the panel):</p>\n    <pre id=\"log\"></pre>\n\n    <script type=\"importmap\">\n      {\n        \"imports\": {\n          \"@triggery/core\": \"/packages/core/dist/index.js\",\n          \"@triggery/devtools-bridge\": \"/packages/devtools-bridge/dist/index.js\"\n        }\n      }\n    </script>\n\n    <script type=\"module\">\n      import { createRuntime, createTrigger } from '@triggery/core';\n      import { installDevtoolsBridge } from '@triggery/devtools-bridge';\n\n      const logEl = document.getElementById('log');\n      const log = (line) => {\n        logEl.textContent = `[${new Date().toLocaleTimeString()}] ${line}\\n${logEl.textContent}`.slice(\n          0,\n          4000,\n        );\n      };\n\n      const runtime = createRuntime();\n      // Expose for ad-hoc poking in the page console.\n      window.__rt = runtime;\n\n      // Trigger 1: tick → notify action.\n      createTrigger(\n        {\n          id: 'demo',\n          events: ['tick'],\n          handler: ({ event, actions }) => {\n            actions.notify?.(event.payload);\n          },\n        },\n        runtime,\n      );\n      runtime.registerAction('demo', 'notify', (n) => log(`notify(${n})`));\n\n      // Trigger 2: required condition gate.\n      createTrigger(\n        {\n          id: 'secure',\n          events: ['secure'],\n          required: ['session'],\n          handler: ({ event, conditions }) => {\n            if (!conditions.session) return;\n            log(`secure ok (session=${conditions.session.id}, msg=${event.payload})`);\n          },\n        },\n        runtime,\n      );\n\n      // Trigger 3: cascade (sync) — a fires b inside its handler.\n      createTrigger(\n        {\n          id: 't-a',\n          events: ['a'],\n          handler: ({ actions }) => actions.goB?.(),\n        },\n        runtime,\n      );\n      createTrigger(\n        {\n          id: 't-b',\n          events: ['b'],\n          handler: () => log('cascade B reached'),\n        },\n        runtime,\n      );\n      runtime.registerAction('t-a', 'goB', () => runtime.fireSync('b'));\n\n      // Trigger 4: handler throws.\n      createTrigger(\n        {\n          id: 'boom',\n          events: ['boom'],\n          handler: () => {\n            throw new Error('intentional boom');\n          },\n        },\n        runtime,\n      );\n\n      const dispose = installDevtoolsBridge(runtime);\n      log('bridge installed — open DevTools → Triggery panel');\n\n      let counter = 0;\n      document.getElementById('tick').onclick = () => runtime.fireSync('tick', ++counter);\n      document.getElementById('async').onclick = () => runtime.fire('tick', ++counter);\n      document.getElementById('cascade').onclick = () => runtime.fireSync('a');\n      document.getElementById('skip').onclick = () => runtime.fireSync('secure', 'hello');\n      document.getElementById('error').onclick = () => runtime.fireSync('boom');\n\n      let sessionToken;\n      document.getElementById('register').onclick = () => {\n        if (sessionToken) return log('session already registered');\n        sessionToken = runtime.registerCondition('secure', 'session', () => ({ id: 'u1' }));\n        log('session registered');\n      };\n      document.getElementById('unregister').onclick = () => {\n        if (!sessionToken) return log('no session to unregister');\n        sessionToken.unregister();\n        sessionToken = undefined;\n        log('session unregistered');\n      };\n\n      document.getElementById('dispose').onclick = () => {\n        dispose();\n        log('bridge disposed (panel status dot should go grey)');\n      };\n    </script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"}}